{
  "requirement": "The SDK formats node inputs using `Contents::format_node_content`,\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprinting.fingerprint_content`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Method on Contents. Both arguments describe the already-read snapshot.\n/// Present these supplied contents as text for an agent.\nfn format_node_content(\n    &self,\n    node: &Self::NodeId,\n    contents: &Self::NodeContent,\n) -> Result<String, Self::Error>;\n```\n\nThe formatter uses the supplied contents; their fingerprint describes the same\nread. For inputs queued on an ask builder, formatting errors return\n`ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node` tool call, a formatting error is\nreturned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue and recover.\n`NodeContent` and `NodeId` retain their application-defined types without\nserialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n- **Use of `Contents::format_node_content` and the supplied contents.**\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` reads a snapshot, then changes the underlying content to \"after\". It asserts that `format_node_content` on the snapshot still returns \"before\", the fingerprint still matches the snapshot, and only one read happened.\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asserts that the formatted contents queued on the ask builder arrive in the request in order. It also asserts that the reads are exactly `[1,3,2,3,1]`, so the formatter is not triggering a reread.\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` and `fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` assert that the formatted text appears in the chat history. The latter also asserts the fingerprint dependencies for the same read.\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` uses a custom formatter (`distinct_pages`) across `read_node` calls and checks the recorded dependency fingerprints.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` shows that the habeas domain formats the supplied contents without resolving the node again. It also checks that an unsupported node kind yields an error.\n- **Formatting errors on queued inputs return `ValidationError::Graph`.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` sets `fail_format` and asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and the agent is not invoked.\n- **Formatting errors during `read_node` return a tool error the agent can recover from.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes the formatter fail. It asserts that the second request carries a `ToolResult` named `read_node` with `is_error` set and the error text, and that the agent then submits successfully. The test asserts no dependencies were recorded.\n- **`NodeContent` and `NodeId` keep their application-defined types, with no serialization or display bounds.** The test `Node` types in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` and `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs` deliberately implement no Serde, Hash or Display. The tests above compile and run against them, which exercises this obligation at the type level.\n\nNo obligation lacks a test, and the assertions check the outcomes the requirement states. The cited `fingerprint_content` requirement is context only, and I did not reassess it.",
  "references": "be8dfa22dce3f9297803609deae03b7b9d0aafd2150eb790d6da62f8e199b8aa",
